<h3 data-start=3D"2301" data-end=3D"2340" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2305" data-end=3D"2340">3.1 Bases de donn=C3=A9es et sch=C3=A9mas</strong><=
/h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2341" data-end=3D"2503">
<li data-start=3D"2341" data-end=3D"2404" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2343" data-end=3D"2404" class=3D"">PostgreSQL permet de cr=
=C3=A9er plusieurs bases dans une instance.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2405" data-end=3D"2503" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2407" data-end=3D"2503" class=3D"">Les bases de donn=C3=A9=
es contiennent des <strong data-start=3D"2444" data-end=3D"2455">sch=C3=A9m=
as</strong> pour organiser les objets (tables, vues, etc.).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"2505" data-end=3D"2536" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2509" data-end=3D"2536">3.2 Tables et relations</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2537" data-end=3D"2726">
<li data-start=3D"2537" data-end=3D"2620" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2539" data-end=3D"2620" class=3D"">Une base de donn=C3=A9e=
s est constitu=C3=A9e de <strong data-start=3D"2577" data-end=3D"2587">tabl=
es</strong> avec des colonnes et des lignes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2621" data-end=3D"2726" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2623" data-end=3D"2726" class=3D"">PostgreSQL est <strong =
data-start=3D"2638" data-end=3D"2653">relationnel</strong>, les tables peuv=
ent =C3=AAtre li=C3=A9es via des <strong data-start=3D"2693" data-end=3D"27=
25">cl=C3=A9s primaires et =C3=A9trang=C3=A8res</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
