 Table</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"3789" data-end=3D"3987" class=3D"">Les <strong data-start=
=3D"3793" data-end=3D"3808">contraintes</strong> sont utilis=C3=A9es pour d=
=C3=A9finir des r=C3=A8gles qui sont appliqu=C3=A9es aux donn=C3=A9es dans =
la table. Voici les principales contraintes que vous pouvez utiliser lors d=
e la cr=C3=A9ation d=E2=80=99une table :</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3989" data-end=3D"4015" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3993" data-end=3D"4015">4.1. <code data-start=3D"4000" data-end=3D"4013">PR=
IMARY KEY</code></strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4017" data-end=3D"4123" class=3D"">La contrainte <strong d=
ata-start=3D"4031" data-end=3D"4048"><code data-start=3D"4033" data-end=3D"=
4046">PRIMARY KEY</code></strong> garantit que les valeurs d=E2=80=99une co=
lonne sont <strong data-start=3D"4093" data-end=3D"4104">uniques</strong> e=
t <strong data-start=3D"4108" data-end=3D"4122">non nulles</strong>.</p>
<pre class=3D"!overflow-visible" data-start=3D"4125" data-end=3D"4209"><div=
