<h3 data-start=3D"2436" data-end=3D"2491" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2440" data-end=3D"2491">2.3. La diff=C3=A9rence entre <code data-start=3D"2=
467" data-end=3D"2479">VARCHAR(n)</code> et <code data-start=3D"2483" data-=
end=3D"2489">TEXT</code></strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2493" data-end=3D"2894" class=3D"">La principale diff=C3=
=A9rence entre <strong data-start=3D"2524" data-end=3D"2540"><code data-sta=
rt=3D"2526" data-end=3D"2538">VARCHAR(n)</code></strong> et <strong data-st=
art=3D"2544" data-end=3D"2554"><code data-start=3D"2546" data-end=3D"2552">=
TEXT</code></strong> r=C3=A9side dans la limite de longueur pour <strong da=
ta-start=3D"2594" data-end=3D"2607"><code data-start=3D"2596" data-end=3D"2=
605">VARCHAR</code></strong>. Cependant, cette diff=C3=A9rence est souvent =
n=C3=A9gligeable, car PostgreSQL optimise les deux types de mani=C3=A8re si=
milaire, et la diff=C3=A9rence de performance est minime pour la plupart de=
s applications. En r=C3=A8gle g=C3=A9n=C3=A9rale, utilisez <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"2828" data-end=3D"2838"><code data-start=3D"2830" data-end=3D"2836">T=
EXT</code></strong> si vous ne souhaitez pas imposer de limite de longueur.=
</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2896" data-end=3D"2899" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"2901" data-end=3D"2925" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
