<h3 data-start=3D"2212" data-end=3D"2253" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2216" data-end=3D"2253">2.3. Types G=C3=A9om=C3=A9triques Support=C3=A9s</s=
trong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2255" data-end=3D"2347" class=3D"">Voici quelques-uns des =
types g=C3=A9om=C3=A9triques couramment utilis=C3=A9s dans PostgreSQL avec =
PostGIS :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2349" data-end=3D"2868">
<li data-start=3D"2349" data-end=3D"2418" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2351" data-end=3D"2418" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
351" data-end=3D"2360">Point</strong> : Repr=C3=A9sente une position unique=
 dans un espace 2D ou 3D.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2419" data-end=3D"2508" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2421" data-end=3D"2508" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
421" data-end=3D"2435">LineString</strong> : Repr=C3=A9sente une s=C3=A9que=
nce de points connect=C3=A9s par des segments de ligne.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2509" data-end=3D"2598" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2511" data-end=3D"2598" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
511" data-end=3D"2522">Polygon</strong> : Repr=C3=A9sente un polygone (une =
forme ferm=C3=A9e d=C3=A9limit=C3=A9e par plusieurs points).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2599" data-end=3D"2643" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2601" data-end=3D"2643" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
601" data-end=3D"2615">MultiPoint</strong> : Une collection de points.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2644" data-end=3D"2698" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2646" data-end=3D"2698" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
646" data-end=3D"2665">MultiLineString</strong> : Une collection de LineStr=
ings.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2699" data-end=3D"2748" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2701" data-end=3D"2748" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
701" data-end=3D"2717">MultiPolygon</strong> : Une collection de Polygones.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2749" data-end=3D"2868" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2751" data-end=3D"2868" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
751" data-end=3D"2763">Geometry</strong> : Type g=C3=A9n=C3=A9rique pouvant=
 repr=C3=A9senter n'importe quel type g=C3=A9om=C3=A9trique (Point, LineStr=
ing, Polygon, etc.).</p>
</li>
</ul>
