<hr data-start=3D"8673" data-end=3D"8676" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"8678" data-end=3D"8698" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
8681" data-end=3D"8698">5. Conclusion</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"8700" data-end=3D"8931" class=3D"">L'isolation des transac=
tions est un =C3=A9l=C3=A9ment cl=C3=A9 pour garantir la coh=C3=A9rence et =
la fiabilit=C3=A9 des bases de donn=C3=A9es dans des environnements concurr=
ents. PostgreSQL permet de g=C3=A9rer cette isolation =C3=A0 l'aide de quat=
re niveaux diff=C3=A9rents :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"8933" data-end=3D"9341">
<li data-start=3D"8933" data-end=3D"9020" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8935" data-end=3D"9020" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
935" data-end=3D"8955">Read Uncommitted</strong> : Non support=C3=A9 (simil=
aire =C3=A0 <strong data-start=3D"8984" data-end=3D"9002">Read Committed</s=
trong> dans PostgreSQL).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"9021" data-end=3D"9110" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"9023" data-end=3D"9110" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"9=
023" data-end=3D"9041">Read Committed</strong> : Niveau d'isolation par d=
=C3=A9faut, prot=C3=A8ge contre les <strong data-start=3D"9094" data-end=3D=
"9109">dirty reads</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"9111" data-end=3D"9220" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"9113" data-end=3D"9220" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"9=
113" data-end=3D"9132">Repeatable Read</strong> : Assure que les r=C3=A9sul=
tats des requ=C3=AAtes restent constants pendant toute la transaction.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"9221" data-end=3D"9341" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"9223" data-end=3D"9341" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"9=
223" data-end=3D"9239">Serializable</strong> : Garantit une isolation compl=
=C3=A8te et des transactions ex=C3=A9cut=C3=A9es comme si elles =C3=A9taien=
t s=C3=A9quentielles.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"9343" data-end=3D"9462" class=3D"">Le choix du niveau d'is=
olation d=C3=A9pend de vos besoins sp=C3=A9cifiques en mati=C3=A8re de perf=
ormance et de coh=C3=A9rence des donn=C3=A9es.</p></div></div></div></div><=
