<h4 data-start=3D"2590" data-end=3D"2623" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2595" data-end=3D"2621">Explication des champs</strong> :</h4>
<ul data-start=3D"2624" data-end=3D"3179">
<li data-start=3D"2624" data-end=3D"2805" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2626" data-end=3D"2805" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
626" data-end=3D"2638">Seq Scan</strong> : Il s'agit d'un <strong data-star=
t=3D"2656" data-end=3D"2675">scan s=C3=A9quentiel</strong> de la table <cod=
e data-start=3D"2688" data-end=3D"2702">utilisateurs</code>. Cela signifie =
que PostgreSQL parcourt toutes les lignes de la table pour trouver les corr=
espondances.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2806" data-end=3D"3041" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2808" data-end=3D"3041" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
808" data-end=3D"2828">cost=3D0.00..15.00</strong> : Le co=C3=BBt estim=C3=
=A9 pour l'ex=C3=A9cution de la requ=C3=AAte. Le premier chiffre (<code dat=
a-start=3D"2898" data-end=3D"2904">0.00</code>) repr=C3=A9sente le co=C3=BB=
t pour commencer l'ex=C3=A9cution, et le second chiffre (<code data-start=
=3D"2975" data-end=3D"2982">15.00</code>) est le co=C3=BBt total estim=C3=
=A9 pour obtenir tous les r=C3=A9sultats.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3042" data-end=3D"3116" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3044" data-end=3D"3116" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
044" data-end=3D"3056">rows=3D100</strong> : Le nombre estim=C3=A9 de ligne=
s renvoy=C3=A9es par cette op=C3=A9ration.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3117" data-end=3D"3179" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3119" data-end=3D"3179" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
119" data-end=3D"3130">width=3D4</strong> : La taille moyenne (en octets) d=
e chaque ligne.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3181" data-end=3D"3208" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3185" data-end=3D"3208">2.3. Types de Scans</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3210" data-end=3D"3296" class=3D"">Les types d=E2=80=99op=
=C3=A9rations de lecture de donn=C3=A9es peuvent varier. Voici les plus cou=
rants :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3298" data-end=3D"3996">
<li data-start=3D"3298" data-end=3D"3479" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3300" data-end=3D"3479" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
300" data-end=3D"3330">Seq Scan (Scan S=C3=A9quentiel)</strong> : Lecture d=
e chaque ligne de la table, g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ralement utilis=C3=A9 si aucun in=
dex ne peut =C3=AAtre utilis=C3=A9 ou si la requ=C3=AAte concerne presque t=
outes les lignes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3480" data-end=3D"3559" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3482" data-end=3D"3559" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
482" data-end=3D"3496">Index Scan</strong> : Utilisation d'un index pour lo=
caliser rapidement les lignes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3560" data-end=3D"3679" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3562" data-end=3D"3679" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
562" data-end=3D"3583">Bitmap Index Scan</strong> : Utilisation d'un index =
combin=C3=A9 avec une op=C3=A9ration bitmap pour effectuer un acc=C3=A8s pl=
us rapide.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3680" data-end=3D"3874" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3682" data-end=3D"3874" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
682" data-end=3D"3701">Index Only Scan</strong> : Utilisation d'un index po=
ur acc=C3=A9der aux donn=C3=A9es sans avoir besoin de consulter la table el=
le-m=C3=AAme (tr=C3=A8s efficace si l'index contient toutes les information=
s n=C3=A9cessaires).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3875" data-end=3D"3996" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3877" data-end=3D"3996" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
877" data-end=3D"3896">Join Operations</strong> : Cela peut inclure des typ=
es de jointures comme <strong data-start=3D"3946" data-end=3D"3961">Nested =
Loop</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"3963" data-end=3D"3977">Merge Join</st=
rong>, et <strong data-start=3D"3982" data-end=3D"3995">Hash Join</strong>.=
</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3998" data-end=3D"4001" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4003" data-end=3D"4035" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4006" data-end=3D"4035">3. Introduction =C3=A0 ANALYZE</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"4037" data-end=3D"4073" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4041" data-end=3D"4073">3.1. Qu'est-ce que ANALYZE ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4075" data-end=3D"4342" class=3D"">La commande <strong dat=
a-start=3D"4087" data-end=3D"4098">ANALYZE</strong> permet non seulement d'=
