<h3 data-start=3D"6718" data-end=3D"6782" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6722" data-end=3D"6782">3.3. Gestion des Pannes dans la R=C3=A9plication Sy=
nchronis=C3=A9e</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"6784" data-end=3D"7084" class=3D"">En cas de panne d=E2=80=
=99un serveur ma=C3=AEtre dans un environnement de r=C3=A9plication synchro=
nis=C3=A9e, un des serveurs esclaves peut =C3=AAtre automatiquement promu p=
our devenir le nouveau ma=C3=AEtre. Cela peut =C3=AAtre g=C3=A9r=C3=A9 avec=
 des outils tels que <strong data-start=3D"7005" data-end=3D"7027"><code da=
ta-start=3D"7007" data-end=3D"7025">pg_auto_failover</code></strong> ou en =
utilisant des solutions tierces comme <strong data-start=3D"7072" data-end=
=3D"7083">Patroni</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"7086" data-end=3D"7089" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"7091" data-end=3D"7156" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7094" data-end=3D"7156">4. Comparaison des R=C3=A9plications Synchronis=C3=
=A9e et Asynchrone</strong></h2>
<div class=3D"overflow-x-auto contain-inline-size"><table data-start=3D"715=
8" data-end=3D"8177" node=3D"[object Object]"><thead data-start=3D"7158" da=
ta-end=3D"7300"><tr data-start=3D"7158" data-end=3D"7300"><th data-start=3D=
"7158" data-end=3D"7190"><strong data-start=3D"7160" data-end=3D"7171">Crit=
=C3=A8re</strong></th><th data-start=3D"7190" data-end=3D"7245"><strong dat=
a-start=3D"7192" data-end=3D"7218">R=C3=A9plication Asynchrone</strong></th=
><th data-start=3D"7245" data-end=3D"7300"><strong data-start=3D"7247" data=
-end=3D"7275">R=C3=A9plication Synchronis=C3=A9e</strong></th></tr></thead>=
<tbody data-start=3D"7444" data-end=3D"8177"><tr data-start=3D"7444" data-e=
nd=3D"7587"><td><strong data-start=3D"7446" data-end=3D"7471">Coh=C3=A9renc=
e des donn=C3=A9es</strong></td><td>Faible (d=C3=A9lai entre le ma=C3=AEtre=
 et les esclaves)</td><td>Haute (garantie de synchronisation des donn=C3=A9=
es)</td></tr><tr data-start=3D"7588" data-end=3D"7731"><td><strong data-sta=
rt=3D"7590" data-end=3D"7601">Latence</strong></td><td>Faible (transactions=
 valid=C3=A9es plus rapidement)</td><td>=C3=89lev=C3=A9e (attente de confir=
mation des esclaves)</td></tr><tr data-start=3D"7732" data-end=3D"7886"><td=
><strong data-start=3D"7734" data-end=3D"7765">Risques de perte de donn=C3=
=A9es</strong></td><td>=C3=89lev=C3=A9s (en cas de panne du ma=C3=AEtre ava=
nt r=C3=A9pliques)</td><td>Faibles (les esclaves confirment les donn=C3=A9e=
s avant validation)</td></tr><tr data-start=3D"7887" data-end=3D"8029"><td>=
<strong data-start=3D"7889" data-end=3D"7904">Scalabilit=C3=A9</strong></td=
><td>Bonne (adapt=C3=A9e aux charges de lecture =C3=A9lev=C3=A9es)</td><td>=
Moins bonne (latence suppl=C3=A9mentaire)</td></tr><tr data-start=3D"8030" =
data-end=3D"8177"><td><strong data-start=3D"8032" data-end=3D"8063">Complex=
it=C3=A9 de configuration</strong></td><td>Simple =C3=A0 configurer</td><td=
>Plus complexe (synchronisation et gestion des r=C3=A9pliques)</td></tr></t=
body></table></div>
<hr data-start=3D"8179" data-end=3D"8182" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"8184" data-end=3D"8204" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
8187" data-end=3D"8204">5. Conclusion</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"8206" data-end=3D"8483" class=3D"">La r=C3=A9plication dan=
s PostgreSQL est un outil puissant pour am=C3=A9liorer la disponibilit=C3=
=A9, la tol=C3=A9rance aux pannes et la scalabilit=C3=A9 des syst=C3=A8mes =
de bases de donn=C3=A9es. Le choix entre r=C3=A9plication <strong data-star=
t=3D"8395" data-end=3D"8411">synchronis=C3=A9e</strong> et <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"8415" data-end=3D"8429">asynchrone</strong> d=C3=A9pend des besoins s=
p=C3=A9cifiques de votre application :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"8485" data-end=3D"8803">
<li data-start=3D"8485" data-end=3D"8637" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8487" data-end=3D"8637" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
487" data-end=3D"8513">R=C3=A9plication asynchrone</strong> est id=C3=A9ale=
 pour les environnements o=C3=B9 la vitesse des transactions est plus impor=
tante que la coh=C3=A9rence absolue des donn=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8638" data-end=3D"8803" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8640" data-end=3D"8803" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
640" data-end=3D"8668">R=C3=A9plication synchronis=C3=A9e</strong> convient=
 aux applications o=C3=B9 la coh=C3=A9rence des donn=C3=A9es entre le ma=C3=
=AEtre et les esclaves est cruciale, mais au prix d'une latence accrue.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"8805" data-end=3D"9022" class=3D"">Les deux types de r=C3=
=A9plication peuvent =C3=AAtre configur=C3=A9s et g=C3=A9r=C3=A9s efficacem=
ent, mais chaque approche pr=C3=A9sente des avantages et des inconv=C3=A9ni=
ents en fonction de vos objectifs en mati=C3=A8re de performance et de disp=
onibilit=C3=A9.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></articl=
