<hr data-start=3D"3665" data-end=3D"3668" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"3670" data-end=3D"3709" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3673" data-end=3D"3709">3. Types de Donn=C3=A9es G=C3=A9ospatiales</strong>=
</h2>
<p data-start=3D"3711" data-end=3D"3825" class=3D"">PostGIS offre plusieurs=
 types de donn=C3=A9es g=C3=A9ospatiales, principalement bas=C3=A9s sur des=
 g=C3=A9om=C3=A9tries et des g=C3=A9ographies.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3827" data-end=3D"3866" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3831" data-end=3D"3866">3.1 Points, Lignes et Polygones</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3868" data-end=3D"4151">
<li data-start=3D"3868" data-end=3D"3963" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3870" data-end=3D"3963" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
870" data-end=3D"3879">Point</strong> : Repr=C3=A9sente une seule position =
g=C3=A9ographique sur la Terre (par exemple, une ville).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3964" data-end=3D"4048" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3966" data-end=3D"4048" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
966" data-end=3D"3975">Ligne</strong> : Une s=C3=A9quence de points qui for=
ment une ligne (par exemple, une route).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4049" data-end=3D"4151" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4051" data-end=3D"4151" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
051" data-end=3D"4063">Polygone</strong> : Un ensemble de lignes qui d=C3=
=A9limitent une zone ferm=C3=A9e (par exemple, un parc, un pays).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4153" data-end=3D"4207" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4157" data-end=3D"4207">3.2 Types de Donn=C3=A9es G=C3=A9ospatiales dans Po=
stGIS</strong></h3>
<ol data-start=3D"4209" data-end=3D"4807">
<li data-start=3D"4209" data-end=3D"4420" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4212" data-end=3D"4362" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
212" data-end=3D"4224">Geometry</strong> : Un type de donn=C3=A9es g=C3=A9n=
=C3=A9ral pour les objets g=C3=A9ospatiaux. Il peut =C3=AAtre utilis=C3=A9 =
pour tous les types de g=C3=A9om=C3=A9trie (point, ligne, polygone).</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4366" data-end=3D"4420">
<li data-start=3D"4366" data-end=3D"4416" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4368" data-end=3D"4416" class=3D"">Exemple : <code data-st=
art=3D"4378" data-end=3D"4401">geometry(Point, 4326)</code> pour un point.<=
/p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4421" data-end=3D"4593" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4424" data-end=3D"4552" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
424" data-end=3D"4437">Geography</strong> : Un type pour les donn=C3=A9es g=
=C3=A9ospatiales sur une sph=C3=A8re (utile pour les calculs bas=C3=A9s sur=
 la courbure de la Terre).</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4556" data-end=3D"4593">
<li data-start=3D"4556" data-end=3D"4593" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4558" data-end=3D"4593" class=3D"">Exemple : <code data-st=
art=3D"4568" data-end=3D"4592">geography(Point, 4326)</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4595" data-end=3D"4807" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4598" data-end=3D"4807" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
598" data-end=3D"4644">SRID (Spatial Reference System Identifier)</strong> =
: Chaque g=C3=A9om=C3=A9trie peut avoir un <strong data-start=3D"4678" data=
-end=3D"4686">SRID</strong> qui sp=C3=A9cifie le syst=C3=A8me de coordonn=
=C3=A9es utilis=C3=A9. Le plus courant est <strong data-start=3D"4755" data=
-end=3D"4763">4326</strong>, qui correspond =C3=A0 WGS 84 (coordonn=C3=A9es=
 GPS).</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"4809" data-end=3D"4812" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4814" data-end=3D"4867" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4817" data-end=3D"4867">4. Cr=C3=A9ation et Gestion des Tables G=C3=A9ospat=
